      en: ["Known as one of the most populous communes in Chile, exceeding 600,000 residents.", "The name 'Puente Alto' refers to a high bridge built over the Maipo River.", "Historically significant for the CMPC paper mill founded in 1920.", "Served by the Las Mercedes and Plaza de Puente Alto metro stations.", "The commune covers an area of approximately 88 square kilometers.", "Connected to the Cajón del Maipo, a popular ecotourism destination."]
